X	diagnostic-reports	p	Your own reports can also go from Finder, in `~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports`. The ones in `/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports` belong to the system: remove those through Console as an administrator rather than from Terminal.
X	diagnostic-reports	p	If an app keeps crashing, update it, and send one of its reports to the developer before deleting the rest. Developers don’t automatically see your crashes: for App Store apps, Apple passes reports on only from people who share analytics with app developers, a setting in System Settings › Privacy & Security › Analytics & Improvements.
