X	document-revisions	p	**Leave the folder itself.** It’s the database of past versions macOS keeps for documents you edit in apps that save automatically, such as Pages, Numbers, Keynote, TextEdit and Preview. Deleting it destroys every saved version at once, and nothing inside can be removed piece by piece by hand.
X	document-revisions	p	**What you can do:** delete versions you don’t need from inside the app with File › Revert To, or drop every version of one big document by duplicating it.
X	document-revisions	p	**Does it come back?** Yes: macOS keeps saving versions as you work, every hour and whenever you save, rename or duplicate a document.
