X	document-revisions	h	How to clear it
X	document-revisions	p	Delete versions you don’t need, one document at a time:
X	document-revisions	li	1. Open the document and choose File › Revert To › Browse All Versions.
X	document-revisions	li	2. Click along the timeline to a version you don’t need.
X	document-revisions	li	3. Move the pointer to the top of the screen to show the menu bar, then choose File › Revert To › Delete This Version.
X	document-revisions	p	To drop every old version of one large document at once, select it in Finder, choose File › Duplicate, delete the original, and give the copy the original’s name. The duplicate starts with no versions. Restart afterwards to give macOS a chance to tidy its store.
X	document-revisions	p	Don’t remove the folder, or anything in it, with `sudo rm`. Besides losing every version, taking pieces out leaves the database out of step with what it stores.
