X	library-logs	p	**Yes, your old ones.** Log files record what apps and installers did, and once they’re a week or so old nobody reads them unless something has gone wrong. Clearing old files from your own `~/Library/Logs` is harmless.
X	library-logs	p	**What it costs you:** the history you’d want when chasing a problem. Keep recent logs, and any report a developer has asked you for.
X	library-logs	p	**Does it come back?** New logs appear as apps keep writing; the old ones are gone for good. “All logs” isn’t something you can or need to delete: macOS’s main log is managed by macOS, which trims it itself.
X	library-logs	h	Measure it
