X	library-logs	li	2. In Finder, open `~/Library/Logs` with Go › Go to Folder and move old files, or a whole app’s folder, to the Trash. Leave the `Logs` folder itself.
X	library-logs	li	3. For reports, use Console: select one under Reports and choose File › Move to Trash.
X	library-logs	li	4. Empty the Trash.
X	library-logs	p	In Terminal, first list the files in your own logs that haven’t changed for over a week, then delete exactly those:
X	library-logs	code	find ~/Library/Logs -type f -mtime +7 -print
