X	deleted-users	p	**Yes, once you’ve checked it.** When an account is deleted and its home folder saved in a disk image, macOS puts that image here. It’s an archive of that person’s files, and nothing on the Mac uses it.
X	deleted-users	p	**What it costs you:** possibly the only copy of that account’s documents, photos and mail. Open the image and look before you delete it.
X	deleted-users	p	**Does it come back?** No. Once the image is deleted and the Trash emptied, the account can’t be restored from it.
