X	saved-application-state	p	**Yes.** It only remembers which windows each app had open, and where, so they reappear when you reopen the app or restart the Mac. Your documents and settings aren’t in it.
X	saved-application-state	p	**What it costs you:** the next time you open an app, it starts with a fresh window instead of your last layout. Save your work first: an app that brings back unsaved windows after a restart relies on it.
X	saved-application-state	p	**Does it come back?** Yes. Apps write their saved state again as you use them, unless you turn the feature off.
