X	preferences-plist-files	p	**Not all of them.** Each `.plist` holds one app’s settings, and macOS keeps its own there too, for the Dock, Finder, keyboard and much more. Deleting the lot resets every app and much of macOS to defaults, for very little space.
X	preferences-plist-files	p	**What one costs you:** that app’s settings. Resetting a single app is a standard fix when it misbehaves, and the reliable way is the `defaults` command with the app quit.
X	preferences-plist-files	p	**Does it come back?** A fresh file with default settings appears as soon as the app runs again; your old choices don’t.
X	preferences-plist-files	h	Measure it
X	preferences-plist-files	code	du -sh ~/Library/Preferences
X	preferences-plist-files	code	ls -lS ~/Library/Preferences | head -10
X	preferences-plist-files	h	How to clear it
X	preferences-plist-files	li	1. Quit the app, and any helper it keeps running in the menu bar.
X	preferences-plist-files	li	2. Find its ID. It’s the file’s name without `.plist`, or Spotlight’s metadata can tell you, as in the first command below.
X	preferences-plist-files	li	3. Delete its settings with `defaults delete` and that ID. Going through macOS’s preferences service means a copy held in memory can’t write the old settings back.
X	preferences-plist-files	li	4. Open the app. It starts with default settings.
X	preferences-plist-files	code	mdls -name kMDItemCFBundleIdentifier /Applications/App.app
X	preferences-plist-files	code	defaults delete com.example.app
X	preferences-plist-files	p	In Finder, the equivalent is moving that single `.plist` to the Trash with the app quit. Don’t delete `com.apple.…` files to tidy up, and don’t empty the folder: that resets Dock layouts, Finder views, keyboard shortcuts and accessibility settings in one go.
X	preferences-plist-files	h	Sources
X	preferences-plist-files	src	Apple: macOS Library Directory Details (Preferences): https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/FileSystemProgrammingGuide/MacOSXDirectories/MacOSXDirectories.html
