X	content-caching	p	**Yes, with the Reset button.** The cache holds copies of Apple downloads kept for the devices on your network. Use Reset in Sharing settings; don’t drag the folder to the Trash.
X	content-caching	p	**What it costs you:** the next update or app that each device needs comes from Apple over the internet again, so it’s slower once.
X	content-caching	p	**Does it come back?** Yes, while Content Caching stays on. Turn it off, or set a cache size, to keep it small.
X	content-caching	h	Measure it
X	content-caching	code	AssetCacheManagerUtil status
X	content-caching	h	How to clear it
X	content-caching	p	Apple’s guide gives the steps for deleting all cached content:
X	content-caching	li	1. Choose Apple menu › System Settings, click General in the sidebar, then click Sharing.
X	content-caching	li	2. Click the Info button next to Content Caching.
X	content-caching	li	3. Click Options.
X	content-caching	li	4. Click Reset, then click Reset again to confirm.
X	content-caching	p	To stop it filling up again, pick one of these in the same place:
X	content-caching	li	- **Set a limit.** In Options, drag the cache size slider or type a figure, then click OK.
X	content-caching	li	- **Move it.** In Options, click Edit next to Cache Location and choose another volume. Caching pauses while the files are moved.
X	content-caching	li	- **Drop the iCloud part.** Set the Cache pop-up menu to Only Shared Content. Apple says all cached iCloud data is then removed immediately.
X	content-caching	li	- **Turn it off.** Switch off Content Caching in Sharing settings if nobody else on the network benefits.
X	content-caching	p	Don’t remove the `AssetCache` folder by hand with administrator rights. It belongs to a system account, and Reset is the supported way to empty it in one step.
X	content-caching	h	Sources
X	content-caching	src	Apple: Set up content caching on Mac: https://support.apple.com/guide/mac-help/set-up-content-caching-on-mac-mchl3b6c3720/mac
X	siri-voices	p	**Yes, in System Settings.** A voice you downloaded for spoken text can be deleted from the voice list. Don’t remove voice files from the system folder they’re stored in.
