X	photos-library	li	2. **Merge duplicates.** Click Duplicates under Utilities in the sidebar, select them and click Merge. One copy stays where the duplicates were; the extras go to Recently Deleted.
X	photos-library	li	3. **Look at videos first.** Videos take far more room than photos, so the Videos album is the quickest place to find ones you don’t need.
X	photos-library	li	4. **With iCloud Photos:** in Photos › Settings › iCloud, select Optimize Mac Storage. The full-size originals stay in iCloud, and the Mac keeps smaller versions when space is limited.
X	photos-library	li	5. **Move it:** quit Photos, drag the library to an external drive formatted APFS or Mac OS Extended (Journaled), open it there, and once it works, delete the original. Apple advises against Time Machine drives, SD cards, USB flash drives and network or cloud storage for a library. If you use iCloud Photos, make the moved library your System Photo Library.
X	photos-library	p	With iCloud Photos on, deleting a photo in Photos deletes it from iCloud and your other devices as well. Look through Recently Deleted before you empty it.
