X	colima-lima-orbstack	h	How to clear it
X	colima-lima-orbstack	h3	First, prune inside the VM
X	colima-lima-orbstack	p	`docker system prune` removes stopped containers, unused networks and dangling images without touching volumes. Colima’s FAQ says space freed this way is released to macOS when Colima next starts (version 0.5.0 and later), so restart it afterwards. OrbStack’s disk shrinks without a restart.
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	docker system prune
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	colima stop && colima start
X	colima-lima-orbstack	h3	Colima: delete a VM
X	colima-lima-orbstack	p	`colima list` shows your profiles. `colima delete` removes the VM but, by default, preserves container data (images and volumes), which is restored when the profile is started again with the same runtime. Add `--data` to delete the instance and all of that data too.
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	colima list
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	colima delete
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	colima delete --data
X	colima-lima-orbstack	h3	Lima: delete an instance
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	limactl delete INSTANCE
X	colima-lima-orbstack	code	limactl prune
