X	docker-raw	p	**No, not as a way to free space.** Docker.raw is the disk of Docker Desktop’s Linux virtual machine. Deleting it removes every image, container and volume at once, databases kept in volumes included, and it must never be deleted while Docker is running.
X	docker-raw	p	**What it costs you:** freeing space the right way, with Docker’s own prune commands, costs only images and build cache that download or build again. Deleting the file costs everything inside it.
X	docker-raw	p	**Does it come back?** Docker Desktop starts again with an empty disk. What was in it doesn’t come back.
X	docker-raw	h	Measure it
X	docker-raw	code	docker system df
X	docker-raw	code	docker system df -v
X	docker-raw	code	ls -klsh ~/Library/Containers/com.docker.docker/Data/vms/0/data/Docker.raw
X	docker-raw	h	How to clear it
X	docker-raw	p	Free space inside the file with Docker’s own commands, with Docker Desktop running:
X	docker-raw	code	docker system prune
X	docker-raw	code	docker image prune -a
X	docker-raw	code	docker builder prune
X	docker-raw	li	- `docker system prune` removes stopped containers, unused networks, dangling images and build cache. It asks first, and volumes aren’t pruned.
X	docker-raw	li	- `docker image prune -a` removes every image no container uses. They download or build again when you need them.
X	docker-raw	li	- `docker builder prune` clears build cache only.
X	docker-raw	p	Volumes only go if you ask: `docker system prune --volumes` adds unused anonymous volumes, and named volumes are only removed by `docker volume prune -a`. Run `docker volume ls` and back up anything you need before using either.
X	docker-raw	p	Docker’s FAQ notes that space is only freed when images are deleted, and gives a command that makes Docker hand the freed space back to macOS straight away:
X	docker-raw	code	docker run --privileged --pid=host docker/desktop-reclaim-space
X	docker-raw	p	To stop the file growing as large again, lower the disk limit in Settings › Resources › Advanced. Docker warns that lowering it deletes the current disk image, so every container and image in it is lost: prune and back up first.
X	docker-raw	p	To start from empty on purpose, use Docker Desktop’s own reset, Troubleshoot › Clean up data, which destroys all containers and images and keeps your settings. Never delete Docker.raw while Docker Desktop is running.
X	docker-raw	h	Sources
X	docker-raw	src	Docker Docs: Docker Desktop for Mac FAQs (disk image): https://docs.docker.com/desktop/troubleshoot-and-support/faqs/macfaqs/
X	docker-raw	src	Docker Docs: Prune unused Docker objects: https://docs.docker.com/engine/manage-resources/pruning/
