X	pyenv-versions	li	3. Remove it with pyenv’s own command.
X	pyenv-versions	code	grep -rs --include=.python-version . ~/Projects | sort | uniq -c
X	pyenv-versions	code	~/.pyenv/versions/3.9.18/bin/python -m pip freeze > ~/py3918-packages.txt
X	pyenv-versions	code	pyenv uninstall 3.9.18
X	pyenv-versions	p	pyenv’s README says you can also simply `rm -rf` the version’s directory, with one caveat: plugins may run extra steps on uninstall that you would then have to do by hand. `pyenv uninstall` is the safer of the two, and it’s one line.
X	pyenv-versions	h	Sources
X	pyenv-versions	src	pyenv README (versions directory, uninstalling Python versions): https://github.com/pyenv/pyenv#readme
