X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	p	**Not wholesale.** Old versions of gems can go with `gem cleanup`, and a Ruby you’ve stopped using can be removed from `~/.rbenv/versions`. Deleting either folder outright removes tools you may still run.
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	p	**What it costs you:** commands that came from gems (`pod`, `fastlane`, `jekyll`, `bundle`) stop working if their gem or their Ruby goes.
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	p	**Does it come back?** No. Gems have to be installed again, and a Ruby has to be built again.
