X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	code	gem cleanup --user-install
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	p	With rbenv, `gem` acts on the active Ruby only. Switch versions and repeat if you keep more than one. To remove a single gem you no longer want, use `gem uninstall` with its name.
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	h3	A whole Ruby you no longer use
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	p	Check that no project’s `.ruby-version` file names it. If you have the ruby-build plugin, it provides `rbenv uninstall`. Without the plugin, rbenv’s README says to remove the version’s directory, which `rbenv prefix` prints. Close any terminal session running that Ruby first.
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	code	rbenv uninstall 2.7.0
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	code	rbenv prefix 2.7.0
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	code	rm -rf "$HOME/.rbenv/versions/2.7.0"
X	ruby-gems-and-rbenv	p	Use one or the other, not both: the last two lines are the manual route.
