X	xcode-archives	p	**Partly.** Archives of builds nobody runs any more can go. Keep the archive of every version people still use: Apple says to retain the archive of each build you distribute, because its debug symbols (dSYMs) are what make that version’s crash reports readable.
X	xcode-archives	p	**What it costs you:** for each archive you delete, the ability to add symbol names to that build’s crash reports on this Mac, and to export or upload that exact build again. Your source code isn’t in it.
X	xcode-archives	p	**Does it come back?** No. Archiving the same code again makes a new build with a different build UUID, and a dSYM only works with the binary it was made with.
X	xcode-archives	h	Measure it
X	xcode-archives	code	du -sh ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives
X	xcode-archives	code	du -sh ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives/* | sort -h
X	xcode-archives	h	How to clear it
X	xcode-archives	li	1. Decide which versions still matter: anything people still run from the App Store or TestFlight, and builds you sent to customers or testers directly. Keep those archives.
X	xcode-archives	li	2. In Xcode, choose Window › Organizer and click Archives. Pick an app in the sidebar to see its archives with version and build numbers.
X	xcode-archives	li	3. Select the archives of versions nobody uses any more and delete them. Or, with Xcode quit, move whole dated folders from `~/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives` to the Trash in Finder and empty it.
X	xcode-archives	p	If you might still look at crashes from a build but want the space, keep just its symbols: open the archive’s package contents and copy the `dSYMs` folder somewhere you’ll keep, named by version and build. When Xcode can’t symbolicate an address, Apple suggests finding the matching dSYM with Spotlight, so keep the copy in a folder Spotlight indexes.
X	xcode-archives	p	If you uploaded symbols with a build to App Store Connect, the crash reports Apple delivers to Xcode’s Crashes organizer already carry symbol names. A crash-reporting service you use may still need the dSYMs, so check it has them before deleting the archive.
