X	gradle-caches	p	**Yes**, with Gradle stopped. `caches`, `wrapper/dists`, `jdks` and the daemon logs are downloads and build data Gradle fetches or makes again. Keep `gradle.properties` and `init.d`: those are your settings.
X	gradle-caches	p	**What it costs you:** the next build downloads dependencies, and perhaps a Gradle distribution and a JDK, before it starts, so it runs slower that once.
X	gradle-caches	p	**Does it come back?** Yes. Gradle also prunes these folders itself, so clearing by hand is mainly for getting space back now.
