X	maven-repository	p	Maven’s docs say you shouldn’t need to do anything with the local repository regularly, except clean it out when you’re short on disk space, or erase it completely if you’re willing to download everything again. Choose how far to go:
X	maven-repository	li	- **One project’s dependencies:** run `mvn dependency:purge-local-repository` in that project. It removes them and, by default, resolves them again; add `-DreResolve=false` to only remove them.
X	maven-repository	li	- **Snapshots only:** add `-DsnapshotsOnly=true` to purge just the SNAPSHOT versions.
X	maven-repository	li	- **Everything:** quit your IDE, make sure no build is running, and empty the folder.
