only removed by `docker volume prune -a`. Run `docker volume ls` and back up anything you need before using either.\n\nDocker’s FAQ notes that space is only freed when images are deleted, and gives a command that makes Docker hand the freed space back to macOS straight away:\n\n```\ndocker run --privileged --pid=host docker/desktop-reclaim-space\n```\n\nTo stop the file growing as large again, lower the disk limit in Settings › Resources › Advanced. Docker warns that lowering it deletes the current disk image, so every container and image in it is lost: prune and back up first.\n\n> To start from empty on purpose, use Docker Desktop’s own reset, Troubleshoot › Clean up data, which destroys all containers and images and keeps your settings. Never delete Docker.raw while Docker Desktop is running.","clear_commands":["docker system prune\ndocker image prune -a\ndocker builder prune","docker run --privileged --pid=host docker/desktop-reclaim-space"],"sources":[{"title":"Docker Docs: Docker Desktop for Mac FAQs (disk image)","url":"https://docs.docker.com/desktop/troubleshoot-and-support/faqs/macfaqs/"},{"title":"Docker Docs: Prune unused Docker objects","url":"https://docs.docker.com/engine/manage-resources/pruning/"},{"title":"Docker Docs: Troubleshoot Docker Desktop (Clean up data)","url":"https://docs.docker.com/desktop/troubleshoot-and-support/troubleshoot/"},{"title":"Docker Docs: Change your Docker Desktop settings","url":"https://docs.docker.com/desktop/settings-and-maintenance/settings/"}],"see_also":["containers","virtualbox-virtual-machines"],"match":[{"glob":"~/Library/Containers/com.docker.docker/Data/vms/0/data/Docker.raw"}],"url":"https://siftmac.com/safe-to-delete/docker-raw","markdown_url":"https://siftmac.com/safe-to-delete/docker-raw.md","published":"2026-11-21","updated":"2026-11-27"}
